From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:02:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: Add iPad Air 2 BCM4350C2

Give the iPad Air 2's BCM4350C2 the Apple board sequence of the iPad 5
and iPad 7: BT_WAKE before BT_REG_ON is cycled, the operational baud
rate set before the patchram, and the LE quirks. That sequence is
validated on those boards, not yet on the Air 2.

Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index d1634b2..3ce92a8 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1688,6 +1688,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id bcm_bluetooth_of_match[] = {
 	/* The iPad 5 BCM4355C0 needs the same sequence as the iPad 7 C1. */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j71t-bcm4355c0-bt",
 	  .data = &bcm4355_j172_device_data },
+	/* The iPad Air 2 BCM4350C2 takes the same Apple board sequence. */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j81-bcm4350c2-bt",
+	  .data = &bcm4355_j172_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j71b-bcm4355c1-bt",
 	  .data = &bcm4355_j71b_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j172-bcm4355c1-bt",
